From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 16:31:57 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 1002/1005] module-raop-sink: default sess.latency.msec to
 whole packets

The default sess.latency.msec is the RAOP latency in milliseconds, which
is not a multiple of the 352-frame (7.98 ms) UDP or 4096-frame TCP
packet, so every RAOP sink logs

  sess.latency.msec ... should be an integer multiple of rtp.ptime 7.981859

and module-rtp rounds the buffer down.  Derive the default from a whole
number of packets instead (rounding up), so the warning only appears for
a user-supplied value.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
---
 src/modules/module-raop-sink.c | 14 ++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/modules/module-raop-sink.c b/src/modules/module-raop-sink.c
index cdede96..399210f 100644
--- a/src/modules/module-raop-sink.c
+++ b/src/modules/module-raop-sink.c
@@ -1913,8 +1913,18 @@ int pipewire__module_init(struct pw_impl_module *module, const char *args)
 		pw_properties_setf(props, "sess.ts-direct", "%d", 0);
 	if (pw_properties_get(props, "sess.media") == NULL)
 		pw_properties_set(props, "sess.media", "raop");
-	if (pw_properties_get(props, "sess.latency.msec") == NULL)
-		pw_properties_setf(props, "sess.latency.msec", "%d", RAOP_LATENCY_MS);
+	if (pw_properties_get(props, "sess.latency.msec") == NULL) {
+		/* module-rtp wants a whole number of packets; otherwise it warns
+		 * and rounds down. Round up instead, plus half a sample so that
+		 * converting back to samples does not truncate below it. */
+		uint32_t samples = SPA_ROUND_UP(msec_to_samples(impl, RAOP_LATENCY_MS),
+				impl->psamples);
+		char latency[64];
+
+		pw_properties_set(props, "sess.latency.msec",
+				spa_dtoa(latency, sizeof(latency),
+					(samples + 0.5) * 1000.0 / impl->rate));
+	}
 
 	if ((str = pw_properties_get(props, "stream.props")) != NULL)
 		pw_properties_update_string(impl->stream_props, str, strlen(str));
